EXPERIMENT 7
Creation of Views, Sequence, Index and Savepoint

AIM
To study and execute SQL commands for creating and using Views, Sequences, Indexes, and Savepoints in a relational database.

OBJECTIVES
• Create a View to display selected data.
• Create and use a Sequence to generate unique numeric values.
• Create an Index to improve data retrieval speed.
• Use SAVEPOINT and ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT to control transactions.

THEORY
A View is a virtual table based on a SELECT query. A Sequence generates numeric values. An Index can speed up retrieval on frequently searched columns. SAVEPOINT marks a point in a transaction; ROLLBACK TO returns to that point.

RESULT
The program demonstrates creation and use of a View, Sequence, Index, and Savepoint.

